Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code contains only diagnosis_tools.py; the GRU4Rec architecture and
final sequence readout are not shown. Diagnosis accesses item embeddings and 
per-position sequence features through a ModelView-compatible wrapper. 
`log2feats(sequence)` produces features used by `predict_score(features, 
items)`. The implementation must preserve causal GRU features and use the final 
nonpadding position for final-history readout with left padding; this module 
does not verify that behavior.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the wrapper, metadata, review data, and 
training histories. Only item embeddings, metadata category lookup, and model 
scoring are actively used. The underlying network is available as `view.model`; 
its `itemnum` bounds valid item embeddings.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with B × L tensors. 
For up to ten batches, diagnosis switches to evaluation mode, computes sequence 
features, scores paired positive/negative candidates, and excludes positions 
whose positive ID is zero.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Sample up to 2,048 real-item embeddings using seed 42,
excluding padding/reserved tokens. Normalize vectors, average off-diagonal 
cosine similarities, and map the result to [0,1]. Higher values indicate 
directional similarity; approximately 0.5 represents zero average cosine, not 
necessarily collapse.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Compute positive minus negative logits. 
Report mean, lower-tail 10th percentile, fraction below zero, and fraction below
0.5. Larger margins and lower failure fractions generally indicate stronger 
sampled training-pair separation.
- **Category breakdown:** Count category occurrences separately for positive and
negative items in low-margin and wrong-rank positions, retaining the top twenty 
categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, masking, ablation, or sensitivity test is 
performed. Embedding subsampling estimates geometry; paired candidate scoring 
measures discrimination.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
collapse, four margin statistics, and nested category counts. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds these into instructions requesting JSON 
with status, core findings, implications, and evidence; it does not itself 
generate that interpretation.

Category metadata is unavailable in this benchmark, so category lists should 
remain empty. Review data and histories are stored but unused. These probes do 
not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, sequence sensitivity, 
gradients, or representation rank. Margins depend on score scale and negative 
sampling; empty valid samples return zeros that can conceal missing evidence.

