Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code contains the diagnosis module, not the GRU4Rec implementation.
Diagnosis examines item embeddings and per-position sequence features exposed 
through ModelView. `log2feats(sequence)` supplies these features; 
`predict_score(features, items)` produces candidate logits. The model’s 
representation computation cannot be verified here. Final inference on 
left-padded histories must select the final nonpadding position; these probes 
instead score all positions with nonzero positive targets.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the view and accesses `item_emb`, 
`user_train`, `meta_data`, and `review_data`; histories and review data are 
stored but unused. The underlying module is available as `view.model`.

The loader yields `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped `B 
× L`. The probe calls `eval()` and scores up to ten batches without gradients. 
Paired candidate IDs have shape `B × L × 2`.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`**: Samples at most 2,048 real-item embeddings 
with seed 42, excluding padding and reserved tokens. It normalizes vectors, 
averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result using `(mean + 
1)/2`. Higher values indicate directional alignment; approximately 0.5 
represents near-zero average cosine, not necessarily collapse.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`**: Mean and tenth percentile of
positive-minus-negative logits over nonzero positive targets. Higher values 
suggest stronger separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`**: Fraction of margins below zero; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`**: Fraction below 0.5; lower indicates fewer 
weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`**: Counts low-margin and wrong-ranking 
positions and lists the top 20 metadata categories separately for positive and 
negative items.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, masking, ablation, or sensitivity perturbation is 
performed. Random embedding subsampling estimates geometric alignment; supplied 
positive/negative pairs test training-position discrimination.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both into instructions requesting a JSON 
interpretation with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog recommendation 
diversity, temporal sensitivity, or generalization. Margins depend on logit 
scale and sampled negatives. Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so 
category lists should remain empty. Empty margin samples return zeros, which 
must not be mistaken for healthy measurements.

