Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The diagnostic code accesses the trained GRU4Rec module through `view.model` and
item embeddings through `view.item_emb.weight`. It excludes padding and samples 
only real item IDs. Sequence representations come from 
`view.log2feats(sequence)`; candidate logits come from 
`view.predict_score(features, items)`.

The supplied file does not show GRU internals or the final-user readout. Margin 
probes score aligned sequence positions rather than explicitly extracting a 
final representation. Any final readout must respect left padding by selecting 
the final nonpadding position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` retains the actual model, metadata, review-data 
interface, and training histories. The implemented probes use embeddings and 
batches from `train_loader`, whose entries are `(None, sequence, positive, 
negative)` with tensors shaped `B × L`.

`run_full_diagnosis` temporarily enables evaluation mode, runs probes without 
gradients, and restores the previous training mode. Nonfinite embeddings or 
valid margins raise errors.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse score:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings using seed 
42, normalizes them, averages pairwise off-diagonal cosine similarities, and 
maps the result to `[0,1]`. Approximately 0.5 means zero average cosine; values 
near 1 suggest directional alignment. This is a geometry indicator, not 
recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Across at most ten training batches, computes 
positive logits minus negative logits wherever input, positive, and negative IDs
are nonzero. Higher mean and tenth-percentile margins indicate stronger 
separation. Lower negative-beats-positive and small-margin rates are preferable;
the small-margin threshold is 0.5.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, masking, removal, or other input perturbation is 
performed. Random embedding subsampling controls probe cost; it does not test 
sequence sensitivity.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned object contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics include
the collapse score, four margin statistics, and a breakdown containing 
valid-position and error counts. Category breakdowns are null because category 
metadata is unavailable. Insufficient embedding pairs or absent valid margins 
produce null measurements.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, temporal 
sensitivity, behavioral diversity, or simulator traits. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis)` embeds measured values and 
definitions into instructions requesting a separate JSON interpretation with 
status, findings, implications, and evidence.

