Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses item-embedding geometry and positive-versus-negative
score separation. The GRU4Rec implementation is absent, so its recurrent 
computation and final sequence readout cannot be verified. Under the task 
contract, final readout must use the final nonpadding position in left-padded 
histories. This probe instead scores features at individual training positions.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view in `self.model` and
accesses `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`; the latter two are unused
by these probes. The actual network is `view.model`.

The probe reads `view.item_emb.weight` and `view.model.itemnum`. For up to ten 
loader batches `(None, sequence, positive, negative)`, with tensors shaped B × 
L, it calls `view.log2feats(sequence)` and `view.predict_score(features, 
items)`. Stacked positive/negative candidates have shape B × L × 2. Positions 
with positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings using seed 
42, excluding padding and reserved tokens. It normalizes vectors, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result to [0,1]. Higher values 
suggest directional collapse; approximately 0.5 corresponds to mean cosine zero,
not necessarily unhealthy geometry.
- **Score margins:** Computes positive logit minus sampled-negative logit. 
Higher mean and tenth-percentile margins suggest stronger separation. Lower 
negative-beats-positive and small-margin rates are preferable; “small” means 
margin below 0.5.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts metadata categories separately for positive and
negative items at low-margin and wrong-rank positions, retaining the top twenty.
These are raw counts, not exposure-adjusted error rates.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbations, shuffling, ablations, or sensitivity tests are 
performed. Embedding subsampling limits computation; sampled negatives provide 
pairwise ranking checks.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, containing 
collapse, four margin statistics, and category breakdowns. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries and requests a separate 
JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications, and evidence.

These training probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, 
generalization, or causal sequence dependence. Margin magnitudes depend on score
scale. Missing valid positions produce zero-valued margin statistics. Item 
categories are unavailable under this task’s data contract, so category 
breakdowns cannot provide supported findings.

