Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe inspects item embeddings and sequence-conditioned positive/negative 
scores through a model-view interface. The underlying trained network is 
accessed as `view.model`; `view.item_emb` exposes its embeddings. Backbone and 
readout code are not supplied, so the final user representation cannot be 
verified here. `log2feats(sequence)` supplies position-level features; any final
readout must respect left padding and use the final nonpadding position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the view and its `meta_data`, 
`review_data`, and `user_train`; only metadata is subsequently queried. 
`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` invokes two probes. Loader batches contain 
`(None, sequence, positive, negative)` tensors shaped B × L.

For margins, the probe switches to evaluation mode, calls `log2feats`, stacks 
positive/negative IDs into B × L × 2 candidates, and calls 
`predict_score(features, items)`. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. 
Computation runs without gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Samples at most 2,048 real-item embeddings 
with seed 42, excluding padding/reserved tokens. It normalizes vectors, averages
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the mean using `(mean + 1)/2`. Higher
values suggest directional collapse; approximately 0.5 means average cosine 
similarity near zero.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Mean and lower 
tenth-percentile positive-minus-negative logits across up to ten batches. Higher
values indicate stronger sampled-pair separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction with negative margins; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction with margins below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts low-margin and wrong-rank 
positions, plus the twenty most frequent metadata categories for their positive 
and negative items separately.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, or sensitivity test is performed. 
Randomness only selects embeddings for the collapse estimate; margins use 
loader-provided negatives.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis)` embeds both into a prompt 
requesting JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`; it does not itself generate that interpretation.

These probes measure training-pair separation, not validation HR@10, temporal 
sensitivity, or simulator traits. Margins depend on score scale and negative 
sampling. Category lists will be empty under this task’s unavailable category 
metadata, although position totals remain meaningful. Empty valid samples return
zeros, potentially obscuring missing evidence. Evaluation mode is not restored 
afterward.

