Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses a GRU4Rec model through `ModelView`; backbone 
internals are not shown. `log2feats(sequence)` returns per-position features 
shaped B × L × H. The probe extracts the final user state at the **maximum 
nonzero input position**, correctly handling left padding; empty histories 
produce zero states. `predict_score(features, items)` supplies actual model 
scores, including learned biases.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses `view.model`, `item_emb`, `user_train`, 
metadata interfaces, feature extraction and scoring. The training loader 
provides `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` tensors shaped B × L. Training 
histories supply frequency counts and temporal examples; unavailable item 
categories are never inferred.

`run_full_diagnosis` uses evaluation/inference mode and seed 42, then restores 
the original training mode and Python, NumPy and Torch RNG states.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings and maps 
mean pairwise cosine to [0,1]. Higher values indicate directional alignment, 
potentially collapse; this does not measure recommendation diversity.
- **Sampled separation:** Across at most ten loader batches, computes 
positive-minus-negative scores at nonpadding positions. Reports mean, lower 
tenth percentile, negative-wins rate and margin-below-0.5 rate. Larger margins 
and lower failure rates indicate stronger sampled training separation. Counts 
and positive-item frequency strata accompany results.
- **Execution checks:** Verify shapes, finite outputs, zero padding features, 
leading-padding invariance, batched/individual scoring agreement and parity with
the module’s `score_candidates`. Failures disable temporal interpretation.

# Perturbation & Tests

For up to 200 eligible training users, select one training target preceded by at
least five retained interactions. Freeze the target plus 99 unique negatives 
excluding the full training history.

Compare unchanged prefixes against oldest/recent/random deletions, local block 
shuffles, final-item removal and last-item-only inputs. Random deletion and 
shuffle each have five repeats. Measure target-rank change, HR@10 change, state 
cosine distance and normalized displacement. Positive rank change or negative HR
change indicates damage; state movement alone establishes sensitivity.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

Returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics include embedding and margin
summaries, `execution_checks`, `temporal_sensitivity`, availability reasons and 
elapsed diagnostic time. Temporal output contains counts, exclusions, per-user 
outcomes, category summaries and length/repeat-target slices. Paired user 
bootstrap intervals require at least 30 complete users.

Four-category macro fields remain null because one view supplies one category. 
These are conditional, in-sample diagnostics—not validation gains or causal 
intent evidence. Null means unavailable. Official macro validation HR@10 alone 
selects models. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds measurements and 
definitions into instructions for a concise JSON interpretation.

