reasonable hypothesis, but the report does not explain how pooled title words 
will avoid reinforcing the broad lexical matches already identified as a 
failure. A scratch-trained encoder has no established understanding of 
compatibility, mood or purpose.', 'The experiment leaves tokenization, 
vocabulary construction scope, text length, encoder dimension, initialization 
scale, projection bias, regularization and missing-text handling unresolved. A 
gate initialized at 0.1 does not guarantee a small residual without controlling 
representation norms.', 'Baseline versus fusion measures the entire 
intervention. A parameter-matched ID-only control and a separately trained 
shuffled-text control would help distinguish useful text information from added 
capacity or regularization. These must remain separate single-model trials.', 
'ModelView compatibility needs a concrete implementation: an effective item 
representation may not expose the embedding attributes expected by existing 
probes. Repeated token encoding for B×L training positions and full-catalog 
recommendations also requires bounded profiling, deduplication or chunking, and 
explicit cache invalidation.', 'The evaluation plan omits validation uncertainty
and adaptive selection effects. Raw logit margins can increase through score 
scaling without improving ranking; they cannot establish better semantic 
discrimination. Sampled HR@10 and feedback from twenty training users do not 
establish full-catalog utility.', 'Originality 3 is plausible, but potential 7 
and difficulty 4 are provisional. The references do not directly establish the 
effectiveness or engineering cost of scratch-trained pooled text fusion in 
GRU4Rec. A baseline-objective comparison may be a cheaper first experiment, 
depending on the supplied loss.'], generating follow-up queries
