Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probes inspect one trained GRU4Rec model through a family-specific view. 
Model implementation is not supplied, so recurrence internals cannot be 
verified. `view.item_emb.weight` exposes item embeddings; 
`view.log2feats(sequence)` returns aligned B × L × H features. Context probes 
select the final **nonpadding position** explicitly, preserving left-padding 
correctness.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the actual `view.model`, histories, 
metadata and review-data interfaces. The implemented probes use embeddings and 
loader tensors; metadata and histories are not directly analyzed.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` clones up to ten batches into CPU snapshots 
containing aligned sequence, positive and negative IDs. It evaluates the model 
without gradients and restores its original training mode afterward. 
`view.predict_score(features, items)` supplies candidate scores. Probes validate
shapes, vocabulary bounds and finite measurements.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real item embeddings, computes 
mean pairwise cosine, and maps it to [0,1]. Approximately 0.5 means zero average
cosine; values near 1 indicate directional alignment.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Reports mean margin, 10th-percentile margin,
negative-wins rate and margin-below-0.5 rate across valid training positions. 
Larger margins and lower error rates indicate stronger sampled separation.
- **Context sensitivity:** Reports paired margin/rank changes and feature 
cosines after history removal, overall and by original history length. 
Sensitivity alone does not establish usefulness.
- **Matched suffix control:** Compares full and cropped contexts on identical 
retained targets, reporting margins, wrong rates and correct↔wrong transitions. 
Position averages are computed within rows, then averaged equally across 
eligible rows.

# Perturbation & Tests

Context sensitivity uses at most 64 eligible rows from two batches, removing 
equal event counts from either end while fixing the latest target pair. Padding 
invariance compares identical real histories under different padding; maximum 
feature error ≤1e-5 passes.

Matched suffix control probabilistically retains between half and all events, 
separating changed and unchanged rows. Dedicated seed-42 generators control 
interventions.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

Output contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including nested context, 
crop and count summaries. Missing measurements are null; category breakdowns and
timestamp strata are unavailable.

These are training-sample, single-checkpoint diagnostics—not validation HR@10, 
full-catalog quality, behavioral diversity or evidence that crop training helps.
Suffix removal also changes target distance. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` 
requests a grounded JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications and 
evidence.

