Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses a sequential recommender through a 
ModelView-compatible wrapper. It reads `item_emb.weight`, obtains sequence 
features with `log2feats(sequence)`, and scores candidates using 
`predict_score(features, items)`.

The backbone and representation computation are not shown. Margin probing uses 
features at individual sequence positions rather than explicitly selecting a 
final user representation. Final inference must separately respect left padding 
and use the final nonpadding position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the wrapper, device, `meta_data`, 
`review_data`, and `user_train`; the latter two are unused by these probes. 
`view.model` provides the actual network and item count.

The margin probe switches the wrapper to evaluation mode and processes at most 
ten training batches containing `(None, sequence, positive, negative)`, each 
sequence-shaped tensor being `B × L`. It converts histories to NumPy, computes 
sequence features, stacks positive and negative IDs into `B × L × 2`, and scores
both candidates. Only positions with nonzero positive IDs contribute.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings using seed 42, 
excludes padding/reserved tokens, normalizes vectors, and averages off-diagonal 
cosine similarities. Mapping this average through `(cosine + 1)/2` yields the 
collapse score. Higher indicates greater directional similarity; approximately 
0.5 corresponds to zero average cosine similarity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Computes positive score minus negative 
score. Larger mean and tenth-percentile margins suggest stronger separation. 
Lower negative-wins and small-margin rates are preferable; small margins use 
threshold `0.5`.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts metadata category occurrences separately for 
positive and negative items in low-margin and wrong-ranking cases, retaining 
twenty leading categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

There are no shuffle, sequence-ablation, sensitivity, gradient, or SVD tests. 
Random embedding subsampling estimates geometry; supplied negative candidates 
test training-position discrimination.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
collapse, four margin statistics, and category breakdowns. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both into instructions requesting a 
grounded JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications, and evidence.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, generalization, or full-catalog 
ranking. Margins depend on score scale and negative sampling. Missing categories
produce empty breakdowns in this benchmark. Empty margin samples return zeros, 
so those values do not establish healthy behavior.

