Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The probe expects a unidirectional GRU4Rec with real-item embeddings, 
`log2feats`, `predict_score`, `_readout`, and `score_candidates`. Features have 
shape B × L × H. The sequence representation is gathered at the final nonpadding
position of each left-padded history; empty histories receive zero states. Model
implementation details beyond these interfaces are not supplied.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
embeddings through `view.item_emb`, and public training histories through 
`view.user_train`. The ModelView adapts NumPy sequences to features and scores 
candidate items. Up to ten loader batches provide `(None, sequence, positive, 
negative)` tensors of shape B × L. Diagnosis runs in evaluation/inference mode 
and restores module modes and Python/NumPy/Torch/CUDA RNG states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Embedding alignment:** Mean off-diagonal cosine among up to 2,048 item 
embeddings, mapped to [0,1]. Higher values indicate directional alignment, 
potentially collapse; this does not measure recommendation diversity.
- **Sampled separation:** Positive-minus-negative score mean, lower tenth 
percentile, negative-win rate, and fraction below 0.5 across valid training 
positions. Larger margins and lower failure rates indicate stronger sampled 
separation. Counts and positive-item frequency strata accompany results; 
unavailable item-category lists remain empty.
- **Execution consistency:** Checks shapes, finite outputs, exact same-tensor 
final-position readout, ModelView/module agreement, padding invariance, 
batching, repeated calls, empty histories, and prediction-entry parity. A 
temporary GRU hook verifies implicit zero initialization. Exported-predictor 
parity requires an explicit adapter.

# Perturbation & Tests
After correctness checks pass, select at most 200 eligible training users 
deterministically. Predict each final training interaction from its preceding 
prefix against 99 fixed unique unseen negatives. Compare intact histories with 
five full shuffles and five shuffles preserving the final item.

Measure state cosine distance/displacement, score RMS movement, margins, ties, 
and—only with the pinned ranking adapter—rank/HR@10 damage. Primary summaries 
retain unchanged draws. Report change accounting, slices, user-reweighting 
intervals, and separate permutation Monte Carlo errors.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
execution checks, temporal records, counts, and runtime; detailed temporal 
artifacts are saved locally. The interpreter requests status, findings, 
implications, and evidence.

These are conditional training-prefix measurements, not generalization or causal
evidence. Missing measurements are null. Four-category macro estimates require 
external aggregation; official validation alone selects models.

