Reflection 1: current report is not sufficient because ['The panel measures 
candidate-distribution sensitivity, but cannot identify why low-frequency 
targets have weaker separation or establish that changing training negatives 
will improve validation HR@10. Frequency matching does not isolate popularity 
bias.', 'Uncertainty is underspecified when a previously frozen uniform set 
becomes draw zero. Its provenance and independence from additional draws must be
verified before applying independent-stream MCSE formulas. Five draws may poorly
estimate maximum-negative-margin variability.', 'Reproduction requires an 
explicit user cap, case-protocol version, ordered candidate pools, serialized-ID
collision handling, and rules for nonfinite draws and empty complete-case 
subsets. The supplied workflow and previous proposals describe different 
target-selection protocols.', 'Exact finite-population calculations could 
replace sampling noise for some statistics: the negative-win fraction has an 
exact pool expectation, and sampled outranking counts follow a hypergeometric 
distribution. Whether full-pool scoring warrants its runtime cost is 
unexplored.', 'The related-work descriptions need primary-source verification. 
Originality 4 is reasonable; future potential 7 is optimistic without a 
prespecified next training experiment, and difficulty 3 understates 
reproducibility and uncertainty work.'], generating follow-up queries
