Reflection 1: current report is not sufficient because ['Masked-mean pooling 
discards word order, negation and attribute relationships, potentially 
preserving the broad lexical associations the intervention aims to reduce. The 
report does not establish that this encoder captures the relevant 
distinctions.', 'ID-only versus frequency-gated fusion measures the whole 
intervention. It cannot distinguish meaningful text transfer from added capacity
or frequency-dependent scaling. Fixed-gate and frequency-bin text-shuffling 
controls would strengthen attribution.', 'The gate is not an identifiable 
measure of text importance: token embeddings and projection weights can 
compensate for small gate values. Report effective residual-to-ID norm ratios 
alongside gate values.', 'Reproducibility details remain unresolved: exact 
tokenizer rules and vocabulary tie-breaking, title/description concatenation, 
metadata-to-item mapping, zero-variance count standardization, initialization, 
and treatment of catalog items absent from training.', 'Compute feasibility is 
unmeasured. Repeated token gathering can substantially increase training and 
full-catalog diagnostic costs; any evaluation cache must be refreshed after 
parameter updates and reconstructed from the selected checkpoint.', 'Originality
