Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The diagnosis targets the trained GRU4Rec model through a host `ModelView`. 
Relevant hooks are `item_emb`, `log2feats(sequence)` and 
`predict_score(features, items)`. Sequence features must retain shape B × L × 
embedding_dim, allowing scores at every aligned training position. The supplied 
code does not show GRU internals or final sequence readout, so it cannot verify 
that inference selects the final nonpadding position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` verifies that `view.model` is an actual PyTorch 
module and retains metadata, review data and training histories. These retained 
data sources are not used by the active numerical probes.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` evaluates at most ten batches of `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)`, with matching B × L tensors. It disables 
gradients and autocasting, temporarily enables evaluation mode, and restores 
module modes and Python, NumPy, PyTorch and CUDA RNG states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding concentration:** Samples up to 2,048 catalog embeddings using seed
42, excluding padding, reserved tokens and zero-norm vectors. It computes mean 
pairwise off-diagonal cosine similarity and maps it to [0,1]. Higher values 
indicate stronger directional concentration; approximately 0.5 indicates 
near-zero mean cosine. This is not a recommendation-diversity measure.
- **Training separation:** Scores each aligned positive/negative pair using 
sequence features, retaining positions where input and both targets are nonzero.
Reports mean margin, approximate 10th-percentile margin, negative-beats-positive
rate and margin-below-0.5 rate. Larger margins and lower error/weak-separation 
rates indicate better sampled training separation, without establishing 
validation accuracy.
- **Support and breakdown:** Counts valid positions, low margins and ranking 
errors. Category lists always remain empty because item-category attributes are 
unavailable.

# Perturbation & Tests

No histories are shuffled, truncated or otherwise perturbed. There are no 
sensitivity, robustness or temporal-order tests. Checks enforce tensor alignment
and reject nonfinite sampled embeddings or valid margins.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The result contains `metrics` and matching `metric_definitions`, including the 
five scalar metrics above and `pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`. Unsupported 
measurements return null with support information where applicable.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds these results into instructions for a 
separate JSON interpretation containing `status`, `core_findings`, 
`key_implications` and `evidence`. Diagnosis does not check validation HR@10, 
predictor/checkpoint parity, routing correctness, recommendation diversity or 
unavailable user/item attributes.

