Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe inspects the trained GRU4Rec model through a compatibility view. 
Relevant interfaces are `item_emb.weight`, `log2feats(sequence)`, and 
`predict_score(features, items)`. The supplied code contains no backbone 
implementation, so the computation of sequence features and final user 
representation cannot be verified. Margin diagnosis uses features at aligned 
sequence positions; it does not explicitly select a final representation. Any 
final readout must respect left padding by selecting the final nonpadding 
position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the actual module as `view.model`, plus 
training histories and metadata references. The loader supplies `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)` tensors of shape B × L. Sequences produce 
features through `log2feats`; stacked positive/negative IDs have shape B × L × 2
and are scored through `predict_score`.

`run_full_diagnosis` temporarily switches the model to evaluation mode, runs 
probes without gradients, and restores its previous mode.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real item embeddings, excluding 
padding. It normalizes vectors, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and 
maps the result to [0, 1]. Around 0.5 means zero average cosine; near 1 
indicates directional alignment. Lower values alone do not establish useful 
representations.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Processes at most ten loader batches. 
Positions qualify only when sequence, positive, and negative IDs are nonzero. It
reports mean margin, 10th-percentile margin, fraction with negative margins, and
fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and smaller error/weak-separation rates 
generally indicate better training-pair discrimination.

Nonfinite embeddings or measured margins raise errors.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, masking, ablation, or sensitivity perturbations run. 
Embedding subsampling uses seed 42; margin measurements use negatives supplied 
by the loader.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics include 
`embedding_collapse_score`, four `pos_neg_*` margin statistics, and 
`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`, which records valid-position/error counts 
and threshold. Category metadata availability is false; category lists are null.
Insufficient embedding pairs or absent valid margins yield null measurements.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds these measurements and definitions into a 
prompt requesting JSON status, findings, implications, and evidence. It does not
itself generate that interpretation.

The probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, recommendation
diversity, temporal sensitivity, or unobserved simulator traits.

